-- title:
--   Finite rational rank of curve-degree profiles on a smooth projective scheme
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, and let $X$ be a smooth proper $K$-scheme equipped with a closed immersion into some projective space over $K$. A probe $t$ is a smooth proper integral $K$-curve with a $K$-morphism to $X$ and two affine charts. For each invertible sheaf $L$ on $X$, define its rational degree profile by
--
--   $$v_L(t)=\chi(C_t,a_t^*L)-\chi(C_t,\mathcal O_{C_t})\in\mathbb Q.$$
--
--   The Euler characteristics are the actual two-chart Cech Euler characteristics in the existing probe definition. The rational vector space generated by all these profiles is finite-dimensional:
--
--   $$\dim_{\mathbb Q}\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb Q}\{v_L:L\text{ invertible on }X\}<\infty.$$
--
--   Neither connectedness nor positive dimension is assumed for $X$; the empty scheme is allowed. This is a degree-profile formulation of the finite numerical-rank consequence of the cited cohomological pairing bound, applied to the finitely many components. It is a derived consequence rather than a literal transcription of Proposition 5.5. The comparison between the concrete Cech degrees and the numerical intersection pairing is included in this assertion. No finite generating set of the Neron-Severi group is assumed.
-- source:
--   Cheng, Ji, Larson and Olander, Theorem of the Base (1 July 2021), Lemma 5.2, p.14, Lemma 5.4 and Proposition 5.5, pp.15-16: https://mattlarson2399.github.io/Papers/theorem-of-the-base.pdf . Derived degree-profile formulation of the finite rational rank of numerical divisor classes, component by component. Curve normalization and finite-map degree scaling identify the existing smooth-curve Cech tests with numerical degree tests; these comparisons remain part of this geometric input. This does not use the proper-scheme Neron-Severi finite-generation theorem being reduced.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicGeometry_CurveDegreeTests
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicGeometry_ProjSpace

set_option autoImplicit false
open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
universe u
attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

theorem AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.finite_curve_degree_profile_span_of_smooth_projective
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (π : X ⟶ Spec (.of K)) [IsProper π] [Smooth π]
    (n : ℕ)
    (i : X ⟶ Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) K))
    [IsClosedImmersion i] (hi : i ≫ ProjSpace.π K n = π) :
    Module.Finite ℚ
      (Submodule.span ℚ (Set.range
        (fun M : {M : X.Modules // Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible M} =>
          (fun t : CurveDegreeTests.Probe π => (t.degree M.val : ℚ))))) := by sorry
